            <ArticleTitle>Chronic total occlusion--a definite state?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Successful recanalisation of a chronic coronary occlusion may result in survival advantage. This report describes a 61-year-old man with an initially chronic occluded right coronary artery. A follow-up angiography 2 years later revealed a spontaneous recanalisation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
